# SIMPLIFY ROADMAP -- refactor pass over `8b53fc2..HEAD`

Goal: run `/simplify` (quality-only: reuse, simplification, efficiency,
altitude) over the hybrid co-sim work introduced between `8b53fc2`
(`feat: add Kanata loop-window pipeline dump`) and `HEAD` (`cd2ce06`).

## Strategy (locked with PM, 2026-06-08 revision)
- **History rewrite (not additive)**: the range `8b53fc2..HEAD` is
  re-expressed as ONE clean commit per feature on top of base `03dfe23`
  (= `8b53fc2^`, so the anchor's Kanata work is included as F13). The
  original 95 commits are replaced; the earlier 8 additive `simplify(...)`
  commits are discarded (kept only on the backup ref below).
- **One commit per feature**, with the `/simplify` cleanup folded into each
  commit (reusing the prior session's `/simplify` results -- already in the tree).
- **Content source = the verified-green tip `c50297e`**: each feature commit
  checks its files out from there, so the rewritten tip tree is byte-identical
  to `c50297e` (asserted via `git diff --quiet c50297e refactor`). Behavior is
  preserved by construction; `c50297e` was 27/27 unit + 18/18 e2e green.
- **Backups**: `refactor-additive-backup`@c50297e (the 8 additive commits),
  `simplify-base`@cd2ce06 and `hybrid`@cd2ce06 (the original 95).
- Docs/plans/config (markdown/yaml/tcl) are not `/simplify` targets; carried
  verbatim into the F15 build (`config.yaml`) and F16 docs commits.

